Marker: INTERVIEW-11-700ea78ef836ec52.

Use a monotonic deque of indices, keeping the largest value at the front. Each index is inserted and removed at most once: O(n) time and O(k) auxiliary space, plus O(n − k + 1) space for the result. Call solve(nums, k) with 1 <= k <= nums.length.

```javascript
function solve(nums, k) {
  const deque = new Array(k);
  const result = [];
  let head = 0;
  let size = 0;

  for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
    // Remove indices outside the current window.
    while (size > 0 && deque[head] <= i - k) {
      head = (head + 1) % k;
      size--;
    }

    // Remove candidates dominated by the current value.
    while (size > 0) {
      const back = (head + size - 1) % k;
      if (nums[deque[back]] > nums[i]) break;
      size--;
    }

    deque[(head + size) % k] = i;
    size++;

    if (i >= k - 1) {
      result.push(nums[deque[head]]);
    }
  }

  return result;
}
```

